.TH C2BTOR 1 "October 2026" "C2BTOR 2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
c2btor \- translate C programs to BTOR2 transition systems
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B c2btor
.I program.c
.B --goto-btor2 --inline
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
C2BTOR uses the CBMC frontend and GotoIR to produce bit-precise BTOR2 models,
with object memory, IEEE-754 circuits and source translation maps.
The default representation is object memory with bit-vector storage.
Runtime object capacities are inferred during model generation.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --goto-btor2-out FILE
Write the BTOR2 model to FILE instead of standard output.
.TP
.B --goto-btor2-map-out FILE
Write PC, GotoIR and source mappings and model metadata.
.TP
.B --memory object|global
Select memory organization; the default is object.
.TP
.B --array bv|array
Select storage encoding; the default is bv.
.TP
.B --memory-object-max-bytes N
Set an explicit runtime object capacity. Exceeding it is a model limit.
.TP
.B --goto-btor2-heap-objects K
Bound total successful allocations; the default is 32. Free does not reclaim identities.
.TP
.B --32, --64
Select the target data model.
.TP
.B --help, --version
Show product help or version.
.SH RESULTS AND WITNESSES
A source SAT result is a counterexample candidate. Use c2btor_witness.py
export, translate and validate for hash binding, BtorSim replay and CPAchecker confirmation.
An UNSAT claim must cover all selected properties and model obligations.
Bounded absence, timeout and unknown are not C SAFE results.
